# ===========================================================================
# .gitignore for the PUBLIC Sutra repository (github.com/startr-trade/sutra)
#
# Copy this file to the NEW repo's root as `.gitignore`.
#
# It does two jobs:
#   1. Ignore build / dev / generated artifacts (normal).
#   2. Belt-and-suspenders: refuse to track INTERNAL content, so even an
#      accidental `git add` cannot leak sales / planning material into a
#      public commit. The PRIMARY guard is that internal files should be
#      physically absent from the public tree (see public-manifest.md);
#      the INTERNAL block below is the safety net.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Rust build output ---
/target/
rust/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# --- Node / JS tooling (VS Code extension, modeler plugin, future UI) ---
node_modules/
dist/
*.vsix

# --- mdBook output ---
book/
docs/book/

# --- Generated impact-analysis catalog (populated on demand by `make catalog` / CI) ---
/catalog/

# --- Python bytecode caches (dev scripts) ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- OpenTofu / Terraform ---
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

# --- OS / IDE ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.project
.classpath
.settings/

# --- Secrets / local env ---
.env
*.log

# --- Claude Code / local dev ---
.claude/

# ===========================================================================
# INTERNAL — NEVER PUBLISH  (safety net: these should not exist in the public
# tree at all; if they do, this stops them being committed)
# ===========================================================================
/STATUS.md
/docs/gtm/
/docs/plan/
/docs/fyi/
/docs/changelog/
/docs/release-notes/
/reference/
/mkdocs.yml
/docker-compose.docs.yml
/scripts/publish/

# The DMN-TCK corpus (OMG ASL-2.0) is cloned on demand for the conformance sweep and must
# NEVER be committed: third-party, ~100 MB, licensed separately from this repo. The harness
# default is <target-dir>/dmn-tck (already covered by target/); these also catch a manual
# clone placed anywhere in the tree.
dmn-tck/
tck/
